From: jayweihung <3034830+jayweihung@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:11:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: a terminal's own icon in the lists (tab.new icon,
 terminal.icon)

A mod that opens an agent (a kit agent, say) can show that agent's own
logo in place of its program's: tab.new {icon} or terminal.icon
{terminal, icon} set the herdr.icon label, an .svg or .png under the
app's folder as a plain relative path (no .., no leading /); agents()
and terminals() then carry it as program.icon, drawn as a picture.
Anything else in the label is ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
