+## `herdr.icon=<path>`: its own icon
+
+A picture shown for the terminal in the lists in place of its program's
+icon (a mod's agent, say, with its own logo): an `.svg` or `.png` under the
+app's folder, as a plain relative path (`data/kit/bots/v2/fox.svg`; no `..`,
+no leading `/`). Anything else is ignored and the program's icon shows.
+Empty removes it.
+
+In the desktop app, mods set it with `tab.new {…, icon}` or
+`terminal.icon {terminal, icon}`, and read it as `program.icon` (with
+`tint` false). The file is read by the client that draws it, from its own
+app folder: write it before setting the label. Clients that don't know this
+label show the program's icon.
+
 ## Adding more
 
 Labels suit small values that change at human speed. Use the `herdr.`
